[b]Disclaimer: this mod was made with AI assistance.[/b] If you're not comfortable with that, please stop reading here.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Essentials/images/banner.jpg[/img]

Common-sense quality of life for [b]Build 42[/b]. Pry doors with a crowbar, open cans without an opener, burn every corpse pile at once, rip all your clothing in one go, save your skills at a mirror for your next life, and handle bandages, flashlights and packed bags with less fuss. Every feature is a sandbox switch, runs on the server in multiplayer, and steps aside when another mod already does the same job.

[table]
[tr][td][b]Game version[/b][/td][td]Build 42 only (42.0+)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Requires[/b][/td][td][b]Dazed Core[/b] 1.3.0 or newer (subscribe to it too)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Multiplayer[/b][/td][td]Yes, the server decides every result[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Add mid-save[/b][/td][td]Yes[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Steps aside for[/b][/td][td]Common Sense, its standalone prying mod, Skill Recovery Journal[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Mod ID[/b][/td][td]DazedEssentials[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Essentials/images/h-pry.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Essentials/images/pry.png[/img]
[list]
[*]Right-click a locked door, reinforced door, garage door or window to pry it open with a crowbar.
[*]Cars: right-click a car for [b]Pry open[/b] and pick a locked door or the trunk, or press V beside one.
[*]Strength raises your chance; reinforced and garage doors are harder. Every try is loud and tiring.
[*]A failed window or car door can break the glass. A pried door loses health and can't be locked again until repaired to full.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Essentials/images/h-minigame.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Essentials/images/minigame.png[/img]
[list]
[*]Hold the left mouse button to push and keep the needle in the green until the bar fills. Run past it and the crowbar slips; three slips ends the try.
[*]A clean, quick pop raises your chance, a botched one lowers it. The server still rolls.
[*]Strength widens the green. Reinforced and garage doors narrow it and make it sway.
[*]The world keeps running. Turn it off for yourself in Options > Mods > Dazed Core.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Essentials/images/h-return.png[/img]
[list]
[*]When an action takes a tool out of a bag you carry or wear, it goes back into that bag once you stop for a moment.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Essentials/images/h-cans.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Essentials/images/cans.png[/img]
[list]
[*]No can opener? Right-click a sealed can for [b]Open with screwdriver[/b]: quiet, but some tries fail and a slip can cut your hand.
[*]Or [b]Smash open[/b] with a hammer or rock: it always gets in, but it's heard and can spill some of the food.
[*]Either can wear the tool. Key-opened tins and unlabeled cans stay vanilla.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Essentials/images/h-burn.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Essentials/images/burn.png[/img]
[list]
[*]Right-click near corpse piles for [b]Burn all corpse piles nearby[/b]: one burn per pile, nearest first, one use of a lighter or matches each.
[*]It skips safehouses you can't use, player-built objects, Dazed machines and containers holding items.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Essentials/images/h-rip.png[/img]
[list]
[*]Right-click any rippable clothing for [b]Rip all clothing[/b]. It queues vanilla's own rip for each item, so yields and XP are the game's.
[*]Takes from what you carry and, if allowed, the containers in your loot window. Worn, held and favourite items and bags holding something are skipped.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Essentials/images/h-mirror.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Essentials/images/mirror.png[/img]
[list]
[*]Right-click any mirror (wall and standing mirrors, mirrored cabinets and dressers) to [b]Remember yourself[/b]: it saves every skill's XP and your known recipes, and makes that spot your respawn point.
[*]After you die, the spawn screen offers [b]Your mirror[/b] first.
[*]At a mirror, the new character can [b]Remember your past life[/b]: each skill comes back to 80% of the saved XP. Skills you already have more of stay as they are. Once per past life.
[*]One save per account in multiplayer, one per player in split screen.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Essentials/images/h-gear.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Essentials/images/gear.png[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Replace dirty bandages:[/b] right-click a clean bandage and every dirty one you wear is swapped for a clean one, with vanilla's own bandaging.
[*][b]Clean with alcohol:[/b] right-click a dirty bandage or rag to soak it in rubbing alcohol or a strong spirit (not beer or wine), 50 ml each. It comes out sterilized, no washing first.
[*][b]Flashlight on your belt:[/b] a flashlight hangs in any belt slot a walkie-talkie fits.
[*][b]Swap hands and back:[/b] one key (unbound until you set it in Options > Mods > Dazed Core) or a right-click swaps what's in your hands with what's on your back.
[*][b]Bags inside bags:[/b] a bag packed inside another bag you carry gets its own inventory button, so you can use it without unpacking it (2 levels deep by default).
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Essentials/images/h-sandbox.png[/img]
Every feature has its own switch (40 options). Prying has options for each kind of door and window, cars, chance, Strength, noise, fatigue, glass, door damage and locks, plus the minigame. Burn all has a range, cans have fail, cut, wear and spill settings, rip all has a nearby switch and an item cap, the mirror has respawn, recipes and the share recovered, and bandages and bags have the alcohol per bandage and how many bags deep to show. Or pick a preset (Easy, Standard, Realistic, Hardcore) on the Dazed Core page to set the prying, can and mirror values at once.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Essentials/images/h-compat.png[/img]
[list]
[*]Build 42 only.
[*]Prying steps aside for Common Sense and its standalone prying mod. The mirror steps aside for Skill Recovery Journal.
[*]Build 42 already opens most cans with a sharp knife and has Fill All at water sources, so Essentials doesn't add its own.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Essentials/images/h-help.png[/img]
Post in the Discussions tab. Include your game version, the mods you run, and your console.txt if there is an error.

